In `factorint`, the test inputs are ordinary positive integers with all default options, so the executed path is the main integer-factorization path: parameter checks near the top, `factordict = {}`, conversion with `n = as_int(n)`, creation of `factors = {}`, setup of `small` and `fail_max`, the `_factorint_small(factors, n, small, fail_max)` call, then either the `next_p == 0` early return or the later `_check_termination(...)` return. Def-use pairs are included only when a tracked variable is assigned on one executed line and then read on a later executed line before any redefinition; variables from branches not taken are excluded.

